- **Uppercase Conversion**: Characters 'A' to 'F' have ASCII values from 65 to 70. Subtracting 65 (the ASCII value of 'A') and adding 10 converts these to 10-15.
- **Lowercase Conversion**: Characters 'a' to 'f' have ASCII values from 97 to 102. Subtracting 97 (the ASCII value of 'a') and adding 10 similarly converts these to 10-15.

This method efficiently handles all valid hexadecimal characters and throws an exception for invalid inputs, ensuring robustness.

