- **Handling Edge Cases**: The solution handles cases where the delimiter is an empty string by splitting the input string at the first occurrence (which is at index 0). This results in an empty string as the first part and the entire input string as the second part.

This approach ensures that the delimiter is not included in the resulting parts and efficiently checks for the presence of the delimiter, providing the required output in constant time relative to the position of the delimiter.

